  "question": {
    "text": "A thin convergent glass lens $\\left(\\mu_{g}=1.5\\right)$ has a power of $+5.0 \\mathrm{D}$. When this lens is immersed in a liquid of refractive index $\\mu,$ it acts as a divergent lens of focal length $100 \\mathrm{~cm}$. The value of $\\mu$ must be",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "Y4ldx",
      "text": "$4 / 3$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ZeJYf",
      "text": "$5 / 3$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    },
    {
      "id": "IFU0v",
      "text": "$5 / 4$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "tUM2y",
      "text": "$6 / 5$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "$\\frac{\\mathrm{P}_{\\mathrm{a}}}{\\mathrm{P}_{1}}=\\frac{\\left(\\frac{\\mu_{\\mathrm{g}}}{\\mu_{\\mathrm{a}}}-1\\right)}{\\left(\\frac{\\mu_{\\mathrm{g}}}{\\mu_{1}}-1\\right)}=\\frac{+5}{-100 / 100}=-5$\n$-5\\left(\\frac{\\mu_{\\mathrm{g}}}{\\mu_{1}}-1\\right)=\\frac{\\mu_{\\mathrm{g}}}{\\mu_{\\mathrm{a}}}-1$\n$\\frac{1.5}{\\mu_{1}}-1=\\frac{-1}{5}(1.5-1)=-0.1$\n$$\n\\begin{array}{ll}\\mu_{1}=\\frac{1.5}{0.9}=\\frac{5}{3}\\end{array}\n$$",
    "image": null
  },
